      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788232574677,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Using Langchain we can do just two line of code, and our code can talk to any model, also calling\nis also same, so we get results also almost similar, so parsing is also easy.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Using Langchain we can do just two line of code, and our code can talk to any model, also calling\nis also same, so we get results also almost similar, so parsing is also easy.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "-naun7FUkU7_fjMuitSoL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 777.6221028477696,
      "y": 8791.974577774046,
      "width": 1210,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2n",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1914903471,
      "version": 372,
      "versionNonce": 1975022201,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788232574677,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In Langchain we can talk with two type of models\n1. Language Models -> these are basically LLM, which will take text input, and give text output as response.\n2. Embedding Models -> these are the models, that take text as input and give response as vector. main usecase\n        of this is semantic search.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In Langchain we can talk with two type of models\n1. Language Models -> these are basically LLM, which will take text input, and give text output as response.\n2. Embedding Models -> these are the models, that take text as input and give response as vector. main usecase\n        of this is semantic search.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
