      "text": "Index ->",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Index ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0cptugMR_6RhS4MUuMCnn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 637.4892903477696,
      "y": 12858.943327774046,
      "width": 1056,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 179460236,
      "version": 1126,
      "versionNonce": 418715513,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788232574677,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Indexes connect our application to external knowledge, such as pdfs, websites or databases\nHere 4 things comes\n\n1 Document Loader\n2 Text Splitter\n3 Vector Store\n4 Retrievers\n\nwe use ChatGPT for out queries and it gives all answer due to it trained on internet data.\nbut there are certain scenarios where ChatGPT can't answer, lets say we are working on a company\nand we have asked ChatGPT, what is the leave policy of my company xyz, or what is the notice\nperiod policy of this company xyz. ChatGPT can't answer due to these are private qus of my \ncompany because it is not trained on this data.\n\nSolution is , we can connect our LLM to external knowledge source, like we can provice rule book\nof our company to LLM.\n\nIf we ask general question like who is PM of India, it can answer by its own if we ask for \nour company then it will take knowledge of external source that we provided, if that has answer\nit can answer.\n\nTo build these kind of applications we can use indexes.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Indexes connect our application to external knowledge, such as pdfs, websites or databases\nHere 4 things comes\n\n1 Document Loader\n2 Text Splitter\n3 Vector Store\n4 Retrievers\n\nwe use ChatGPT for out queries and it gives all answer due to it trained on internet data.\nbut there are certain scenarios where ChatGPT can't answer, lets say we are working on a company\nand we have asked ChatGPT, what is the leave policy of my company xyz, or what is the notice\nperiod policy of this company xyz. ChatGPT can't answer due to these are private qus of my \ncompany because it is not trained on this data.\n\nSolution is , we can connect our LLM to external knowledge source, like we can provice rule book\nof our company to LLM.\n\nIf we ask general question like who is PM of India, it can answer by its own if we ask for \nour company then it will take knowledge of external source that we provided, if that has answer\nit can answer.\n\nTo build these kind of applications we can use indexes.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
